<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vyazma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vyazma is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the Vyazma river on the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> to Smolensk. Seat of a small principality from the 13th century, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in 1403 and by Moscow in 1494. Russian forces fought the retreating French there in 1812, and in October 1941 Soviet armies were encircled nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vyazma.jpg" alt="Vyazma" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stoljaroff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyh%C3%A4n_Kolminaisuuden_kirkko_Vjazmassa_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
